  "core_idea": "**Herself** refers back to a woman, girl, or female animal already mentioned, either as the object of her own action or to show that she, no one else, did it.",
  "senses": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "signpost": "reflexive",
      "definition": "used as the object of a verb or preposition when the action affects a woman, girl, or female animal already mentioned, the same one who is the subject",
      "explanation": "**Herself** is used when the subject and the object of the same clause refer to the same female person or animal: *she cut herself*. It is not just another way of saying **her**: when the object is a different person from the subject, use **her** (*he gave it to her*).",
